#DESCRIPTION
Force-free current sheet magnetic reconnection benchmark (Le et al. 2016)
with the FULL-PIC EM solver (solveEM = T, Maxwell/GMRES): kinetic ions and electrons.

Scale and Grid Calculation:
  FLEKS uses Gaussian / CGS-normalized code units where:
    curl(B) = 4*pi*J,  d_i = v_A / Omega_ci = 1/sqrt(4*pi) ~ 0.2820948 code units
    P_mag = B0^2 / (8*pi) = 1/(8*pi) ~ 0.0397887 code units
  Domain: Lx = 20 d_i = 20 * 0.2820948 ~ 5.6419 code units  (x in [-2.82095, 2.82095])
          Ly = 10 d_i = 10 * 0.2820948 ~ 2.82095 code units  (y in [-1.41047, 1.41047])
  Sheet half-width: lambda = 1.0 d_i = 0.2821 code units
  Grid: 64 x 32 (dx = dy = 0.3125 d_i ~ 0.08815 code units, isotropic square cells)
  Temperatures:
    beta_i = 0.50 -> Pi_code = 0.25 / (4*pi) ~ 0.01989 code units -> T_i = 24191.0 K
    beta_e = 0.10 -> Pe_code = 0.05 / (4*pi) ~ 0.00398 code units -> T_e = 4838.2 K (Ti/Te = 5)

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-2.82095                xMin  [code units; Lx = 20 d_i = 5.6419 code units]
 2.82095                xMax
-1.41047                yMin  [code units; Ly = 10 d_i = 2.82095 code units]
 1.41047                yMax
-0.5                    zMin  [thin invariant direction, 1 cell]
 0.5                    zMax

#NCELL
64                      nCellX
32                      nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
32                      maxBlockSizeX
16                      maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
F                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

#FIELDBOXBOUNDARY
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryLo  (x)
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryHi
conducting              fieldBoxBoundaryLo  (y)
conducting              fieldBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryLo  (z)
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryHi

#PARTICLEBOXBOUNDARY
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryLo
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryHi
reflect                 particleBoxBoundaryLo
reflect                 particleBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryLo
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryHi

#SOLVEEM
T                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
F                       useHybridPIC

#PLASMA
2                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass           Species 0: ions
1.0                     charge
0.04                    mass           Species 1: electrons (mi/me = 25)
-1.0                    charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
65.15939                rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: ions (n_i = 1.0)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
24191.0                 T [K]          ions, beta_i = 0.5, Ti_code = 0.25 / (4*pi)
2.6063756               rho [amu/cc]   Species 1: electrons (rho_e = rho_i * me/mi = 65.15939 * 0.04)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
4838.2                  T [K]          electrons, beta_e = 0.1, Te_code = 0.05 / (4*pi), Ti/Te = 5
0.0                     bx [T]         set by ForceFreeIC
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

#TESTCASE
forcefree

#FORCEFREEIC
0.2821                  lambda   [current sheet half-width = 1.0 d_i = 1/sqrt(4*pi) code units]
1.0                     b0       [asymptotic in-plane field B0]
0.3                     bg       [guide field ratio Bg/B0 = 0.3]
0.05                    perturb  [initial perturbation amplitude dB/B0 = 0.05]

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.01                    dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI  [m; lNorm = 100 km ~ d_i]
1.0e5                   uNormSI  [m/s; uNorm = 100 km/s ~ vA, tNorm = 1 s]

#MONITOR
50                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
10                      dnSavePic
10                      dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
10                      nParticle per cell in X
10                      nParticle per cell in Y
1                       nParticle per cell in Z

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 fluid ascii pic     plotString
-1                      dn
0.5                     dt
1                       dx

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
1.0                     TimeMax

#RUN
